    "result_text": "Build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: when a newly computed `customerCode` collides with an existing owner's `customerCode`, append `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\nI kept structural impact minimal by adding behaviour as a new cohesive unit rather than growing an existing method/class:\n\n1. **New function class** `DeduplicateOwnerCustomerCode` \u2014 a single-method class (so `WMC_other` is effectively 0), it gathers the codes taken by *other* owners and, if the assigned code collides, walks `n = 2, 3, \u2026` until it finds a free `base-<n>`. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` (which carries the SHA-256/region complexity) is left completely untouched.\n\n2. **One YAML step** wired into `owners.POST.yml` right after `assignCustomerCode`, under the same `transaction` governance, so de-duplication happens against committed owners before save.\n\nThe existing acceptance test `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` (distinct owners get distinct codes) passes, and the full suite is green.",
